# The majors' sittings (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Several players"): while Every Name's council sits
# (sitting:every_name.first, then .second), a Haven leader can be talked round before the tally.
# A sway is the vote's own (RZ_QuestVote): one per player per sitting, the speaker's own vote if they
# have one, only for an option on the table. A failed persuade is a branch, never a dead end.

conv haven.sitting.first
for seat:haven/council_head, stronghold:haven
when sitting:every_name.first & !swayed:every_name.first
topic "What's the council voting on?"
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say The council sits at supper tonight: a head from every house, round one pot. They're voting on how the Haven eats when there isn't enough for everyone.
  say Every head brings a count and a worry, and the worry's always the same: mouths. Say your piece to me now, if you've got one. At the table, nobody hears anybody.
  > @pot Everyone eats. Say that at the table. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.first.pot   check persuade haven 2 bg:elder,nurse   do sway:every_name.first.pot
  > @workers Houses that work should eat first. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.first.workers   check persuade haven 2 bg:elder,soldier   do sway:every_name.first.workers
  > @cards Take Bastion's cards. They're fair. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.first.cards   check persuade haven 3 bg:police,soldier   do sway:every_name.first.cards
  > @tins Keep the stores full. Don't ask how. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.first.tins   check persuade haven 3 bg:excon,raider   do sway:every_name.first.tins
  > @listen I'll just listen tonight. -> listen

node moved
  say That's not nothing. I'll say it at the table, in my own words. They'll know whose words they were, mind, and some of them will look at you.
  > @back1 Thank you. That's all I ask. -> hub

node short
  say I hear you. I don't agree, quite. I'll think about it on the walk over, which is as far as thinking goes these days.
  > @back2 That's fair. Something else. -> hub

node refused
  say No. I know my house, and you know the road. Sit at the end tonight and listen, and see if you still think so after.
  > @back3 I'll come and listen. -> hub

node listen
  say Then listen. Whatever they decide, somebody walks out of a house because of it. Remember that when you eat.
  > @back4 I'll remember. -> hub

conv haven.sitting.second
for seat:haven/council_head, stronghold:haven
when sitting:every_name.second & !swayed:every_name.second
topic "The council's sitting again?"
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say We sit again tonight. Keep the rule we made, or change it. The hungry week has already answered half the question for us, and not kindly.
  say Everyone saw who went thin, and who didn't. Say your piece now if you want it carried in.
  > @pot Everyone eats. Still. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.second.pot   check persuade haven 2 bg:elder,nurse   do sway:every_name.second.pot
  > @workers Work first, then eat. It held. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.second.workers   check persuade haven 2 bg:elder,soldier   do sway:every_name.second.workers
  > @cards Keep Bastion's ration cards. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.second.cards   check persuade haven 3 bg:police,soldier   do sway:every_name.second.cards
  > @tins Keep the Thursday arrangement. -> moved | short | refused   if tabled:every_name.second.tins   check persuade haven 3 bg:excon,raider   do sway:every_name.second.tins
  > @listen I'll just listen tonight. -> listen

node moved
  say All right. I'll carry it in. If it goes badly, it was my idea. If it goes well, it was also my idea.
  > @back1 Thank you. Something else. -> hub

node short
  say Maybe. I'll see who's hungry tonight. That decides more votes than speeches do.
  > @back2 That's fair. Something else. -> hub

node refused
  say No. You weren't here for the hungry week, not the way we were. Come to the table anyway. You should see it.
  > @back3 I'll come and see it. -> hub

node listen
  say Then you'll hear the whole house argue about bread. That's the Haven: bread, and who isn't here to eat it.
  > @back4 I'll be there. -> hub
